From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:44:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 062/111] Synchronized views also scroll sideways together

With "Synchronize scrolling" on, scrolling one view sideways (wheel, scrollbar
or a cursor moving past the edge) now moves the other view by the same
distance, as vertical scrolling moves it by the same number of lines. The
other view stops at its left edge and where its widest visible line ends.
A scroll is reported to the views when its horizontal part changes too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

